    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nWhen `vim.loader` is enabled, the LSP tagfunc throws an error\n\n### Steps to reproduce using \"nvim --clean -u minimal_init.lua\"\n\nUse the example `minimal_init.lua` but put `vim.loader.enable()` at the beginning, for example:\n\n```lua\nvim.loader.enable()\n\nlocal pattern = 'python'\nlocal cmd = { 'pylsp' }\nlocal root_markers = { '.git', '.editorconfig' }\nlocal settings = vim.empty_dict()\n\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('FileType', {\n\tpattern = pattern,\n\tcallback = function(args)\n\t\tlocal match = vim.fs.find(root_markers, { path = args.file, upward = true })[1]\n\t\tlocal root_dir = match and vim.fn.fnamemodify(match, ':p:h') or nil\n\t\tvim.lsp.start({\n\t\t\tname = 'pylsp',\n\t\t\tcmd = cmd,\n\t\t\troot_dir = root_dir,\n\t\t\tsettings = settings\n\t\t})\n\tend\n})\n```\n\nThen go to any file and press `CTRL-]` on a variable/function name\n\nYou get the error:\n```\nE5108: Lua: /usr/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/_tagfunc.lua:13: attempt to call field '_get_line_byte_from_position' (a nil value)\nstack traceback:\n        /usr/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/_tagfunc.lua:13: in function 'mk_tag_item'\n        /usr/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/_tagfunc.lua:32: in function 'add'\n        /usr/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/_tagfunc.lua:51: in function 'query_definition'\n        /usr/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/_tagfunc.lua:91: in function </usr/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp/_tagfunc.lua:86>\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nIt should go to definition\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev+934-6a6431cb99\n\n### Language server name/version\n\nAny, but pylsp v1.14.0 in this example\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nFedora 44\n\n### Log file\n\n_No response_",
