        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "If you test-drive nightly and update regularly, it can be that the `luac` cache gets stale (this is _very_ rare; I've never seen it personally). If you use it (either explicitly or by using `lazy.nvim`), always manually wipe the cache first and try again (`~/.cache/nvim/luac` on POSIX). The stacktrace points towards a function call that was removed in May so definitely should not be part of the version you specify.\n\n(Maybe a tiny `vim.loader.clear()` endpoint can nudge people towards doing that _before_ opening an issue. There's `vim.loader.reset()` but it's not clear -- from the docs nor from a brief glance at the implementation -- what it does.)\n\n(Off-topic: For me, `vim.loader` yields about 15% startuptime improvement on macOS according to `hyperfine -w 5 -m 500 \"nvim +q\"` -- and that is with most plugins loaded on-demand so only 4 active plugins. Definitely makes a positive difference.)",
